A||||11||Hank is Here||It may be fraud but.....||||1||
Z||000000||Hank is Here||12-15-2000||11:32 PM||||I just got my 87 GT back from the bodyshop yesterday.  Just for the record $1600 will not total an 87 GT.  What I am thinking is I want to transfer the vin tag from my fender to the replacement fender on the car now.  Has anyone attempted this?  How was it accomplished?  I am aware that this is not exactly "legal" but I want to see if it is possible.  <P>Mark Johnson||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-16-2000||12:59 AM||||HIGHLY illegal....VERY difficult to do.. VERY noticable when done...basically what Im saying is....<BR><B> DON'T DO IT!!!</B>||||reg||11
Z||000002||RNGCRSH||12-16-2000||01:36 AM||||Not ilegal. The only vin tags that are legal identifiers for the car are the one on the dash and the one under the left speaker. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-16-2000||01:54 AM||||I never understood the big deal about swapping bodt panels... if you install a body kit, wouldn't that mean most of the panels with VINs are now gone completely?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||12-16-2000||02:00 AM||||Not illegal, but unethical.  This will cause the car to appear like the body parts are original.  This is a tough feat anyway, but why go to all that trouble just to fool others into thinking this is original?||||reg||9
Z||000005||RNGCRSH||12-16-2000||01:01 PM||||If its the tag from the left inner fender with all the codes, then I would swap it, any others I wouldn't bother with. just make sure to remove the vin tags that do not match you car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-16-2000||04:21 PM||||According to my friends, former officers on 2 area police forces, it is a major ass crime to remove OE VIN tags from any part of the car. It's a federal thing not up to the states.<P>The tags are made to be permanent parts of whatever they are attached to. You can't peal them off without destroying them.<P>If VIN taged parts are put on your car make sure you are given detailed reciepts, including those numbers.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RNGCRSH||12-16-2000||04:33 PM||||Sorry Ogre, but I think your friends are wrong. I have done this many times with other vehicles and disclosed it to the DMV when regestering the vehicle. The original post is refering to a sticker. not a vin tag, Once again the only legal vin identifiers on a car are those that are stamped in metal and riveted down, I restored a '76 Vette once to mint condition including every grease pencil mark like it would be from the factory. I had to replace the cross member the vin tag was on. I swaped the vin tag to the new cross member. That is a totaly legal swap If all of the numbers on your car match then there is no violation of the law state or federal.<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||12-16-2000||05:17 PM||||It's just a sticker!  Use some type of adhesive remover and do it.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phaeton||12-16-2000||11:22 PM||||Hmm, the vin sticker on my Fiero's nose was so loose I pulled it off and stuck it on my monitor for safe keeping.<BR>I always figgered it was just put on poorly, but now you guys got me thinking the Fiero was probably in a wreck and the previous owner swapped the sticker over with some cheap adhesive.<BR>Either way I'm glad to have the complete set of panel stickers.||||reg||12
Z||000010||Cooter||12-16-2000||11:30 PM||||On the wrecked cars we build, the state inspectors will burn our tails if we were to do something like that. The stickers are there to identify replacement parts or stolen parts etc... It is not worth the trouble it could get you if tamper with the id tags. But laws vary from state to state, so suit yourself.||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||12-17-2000||03:44 PM||||this is how it is in ohio anyway. any new or aftermarket parts come with a new sn# attached to it and a tear off that you put in glovebox,under hood or trunk to prove that you were the original part purchaser and it wasnt stolen. When I put on used parts with vin # the salvage yard is supposed to supply you with paperwork to prove the part # they sold you. If you rebuild a total even, when the Highway Patrol inspects it for re registration all you have to do is have the stickers on new parts, reciepts from salvage yard. You cannot legally remove the one on dash the original has to stay on it. Now the question on that is what if you install a used dash from yard.......that one I cant answer.||||reg||1
